WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.359 --> 00:00:05.790
An SCP Foundation researcher is monitoring
the salt content of a large tank filled with

00:00:05.790 --> 00:00:07.030
water.

00:00:07.030 --> 00:00:11.509
Inside the tank just under the surface is
a huge mass of rusted metal, though a few

00:00:11.509 --> 00:00:16.630
pieces have a couple specks of their original
shiny surface visible through the dark red

00:00:16.630 --> 00:00:17.630
exterior.

00:00:17.630 --> 00:00:21.980
The researcher suddenly looks up from his
task though, does anyone else hear that noise?

00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:27.250
It’s a terrible noise, like metal pieces
scraping and scratching against each other.

00:00:27.250 --> 00:00:30.490
But the heap of metal in the tank isn’t
moving.

00:00:30.490 --> 00:00:35.460
Still the noises continue though, and as the
researcher keeps staring at the unmoving hunk

00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:41.480
of metal in the tank, all he can think about
is diving in and letting his body become a

00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:42.870
part of it…

00:00:42.870 --> 00:00:48.040
Kept submerged in a big saltwater tank at
the SCP Foundation, is an object, but perhaps

00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:51.780
a more accurate way to describe it would be
as a machine.

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:57.360
Referred to as SCP-882, the machine’s containment
tank is required, according to containment

00:00:57.360 --> 00:01:02.360
procedures, to be filled with at least forty
percent pure sea water, direct from the ocean.

00:01:02.360 --> 00:01:08.220
If, at any point, the rusty surface of SCP
882 begins to show signs of becoming more

00:01:08.220 --> 00:01:14.310
like shiny metal, then the percentage of sea
water must be raised to 100% until the metal

00:01:14.310 --> 00:01:16.390
is completely covered in rust.

00:01:16.390 --> 00:01:18.070
Trying to keep metal rusted?

00:01:18.070 --> 00:01:23.270
That might sound like a strange concept, but
you’ll see why it’s so necessary soon.

00:01:23.270 --> 00:01:29.620
SCP-882 looks like little more than a collection
of seemingly random pieces of metal, all fused

00:01:29.620 --> 00:01:31.810
together as if they had been welded.

00:01:31.810 --> 00:01:38.390
Gears, cables, pulleys, screws and belts,
all different shapes and sizes, all made of

00:01:38.390 --> 00:01:39.870
different metals.

00:01:39.870 --> 00:01:44.380
All of these various components do not appear
to be uniform, or to have been made to fit

00:01:44.380 --> 00:01:51.020
each other, and are instead all stuck together
in one big, unstructured mass of metal objects.

00:01:51.020 --> 00:01:54.450
But SCP-882 wasn’t built to be like this.

00:01:54.450 --> 00:02:00.640
Instead, this seems to be the result of one
of SCP-882’s latent anomalous properties:

00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:02.820
the absorption of metal.

00:02:02.820 --> 00:02:08.170
Any metal that comes into contact with SCP-882
will become permanently attached to it, and

00:02:08.170 --> 00:02:12.670
after a few days, will be a new part of SCP-882.

00:02:12.670 --> 00:02:18.900
That means that any metal that touches that
new piece will also become a part of SCP-882,

00:02:18.900 --> 00:02:21.050
and on and on.

00:02:21.050 --> 00:02:27.260
Because of this strange property, absolutely
no metal is allowed to be brought near SCP-882,

00:02:27.260 --> 00:02:31.670
and only organic materials are permitted to
come into direct contact with it.

00:02:31.670 --> 00:02:36.600
That includes using non-metal alternatives
to keep the machine securely contained.

00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:42.080
SCP-882 is suspended in its salt water tank
by organic cotton fiber lines, which also

00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:44.770
require changing on a daily basis.

00:02:44.770 --> 00:02:49.600
Any and all researchers that the SCP Foundation
has interacting with the metallic mass are

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:53.170
required to wear thick cotton gloves at all
times.

00:02:53.170 --> 00:02:56.190
You might think that this sounds pretty easy
to contain.

00:02:56.190 --> 00:02:58.060
Just don’t let it touch metal?

00:02:58.060 --> 00:02:59.239
No problem.

00:02:59.239 --> 00:03:00.530
Organic materials only?

00:03:00.530 --> 00:03:02.220
No removal of rust allowed?

00:03:02.220 --> 00:03:03.220
No sweat.

00:03:03.220 --> 00:03:07.420
The Foundation staff working with 882 probably
felt the same way.

00:03:07.420 --> 00:03:11.270
Until they started hearing SCP-882 make noise.

00:03:11.270 --> 00:03:17.310
While SCP-882 is usually silent, personnel
that spend an extended period of time close

00:03:17.310 --> 00:03:22.890
to the machine have reported intense grinding
or clicking noises coming from somewhere in

00:03:22.890 --> 00:03:24.640
the mess of metal components.

00:03:24.640 --> 00:03:31.239
While they start out low and are almost unnoticeable,
these sounds get gradually louder until eventually,

00:03:31.239 --> 00:03:35.670
they become completely unbearable for human
beings to withstand.

00:03:35.670 --> 00:03:38.620
So then why don’t these sounds show up on
audio recordings?

00:03:38.620 --> 00:03:44.900
Because the grinding or clicking noises from
SCP 882 are, in actuality, extreme auditory

00:03:44.900 --> 00:03:50.180
hallucinations, but even though they aren’t
real, these sounds are more than capable of

00:03:50.180 --> 00:03:53.650
driving anyone who hears them into a state
of psychosis.

00:03:53.650 --> 00:03:56.099
And here’s where things get tricky.

00:03:56.099 --> 00:04:01.909
The only way to make the noises stop… is
to offer SCP 882 more metal.

00:04:01.909 --> 00:04:06.330
As mentioned, any object that is made of any
type of metal that comes into contact with

00:04:06.330 --> 00:04:09.630
the machine becomes a part of its mass.

00:04:09.630 --> 00:04:14.349
Allowing new objects to become fused to the
surface of SCP-882 will cause the grinding

00:04:14.349 --> 00:04:20.239
noises to subside, but will increase SCP-882’s
mass permanently.

00:04:20.239 --> 00:04:24.199
If the noises aren’t stopped though, then
the mental state of those afflicted by them

00:04:24.199 --> 00:04:30.759
only grows worse, and some victims of SCP-882’s
auditory hallucinations have gone so far as

00:04:30.759 --> 00:04:36.400
to throw themselves into the tank containing
it, where they were killed almost immediately,

00:04:36.400 --> 00:04:40.870
their bodies crushed to death by anomalous
forces and becoming unrecoverable from the

00:04:40.870 --> 00:04:44.280
tangle of gears and random metal objects.

00:04:44.280 --> 00:04:49.779
The SCP Foundation now requires any of its
personnel that work directly with SCP-882

00:04:49.779 --> 00:04:53.580
to report any instances of noise coming from
the machine.

00:04:53.580 --> 00:04:59.080
Additionally, whoever reports hearing strange
sounds in the vicinity of SCP-882 must turn

00:04:59.080 --> 00:05:02.659
themselves in for a full psychological evaluation.

00:05:02.659 --> 00:05:07.351
Depending on the results, the researcher will
either be free to return to their work, or

00:05:07.351 --> 00:05:12.009
will face containment themselves at an undisclosed
Foundation facility.

00:05:12.009 --> 00:05:17.180
The surface of SCP-882 exhibits an extreme
resistance to damage.

00:05:17.180 --> 00:05:20.999
According to the Foundation’s testing, the
metal structure has a tensile strength and

00:05:20.999 --> 00:05:24.740
toughness stronger than aircraft grade titanium
alloy.

00:05:24.740 --> 00:05:30.939
Despite this, the machine seems to still be
constructed of weaker metals like tin, iron,

00:05:30.939 --> 00:05:33.180
gold and many others still yet to be identified.

00:05:33.180 --> 00:05:38.439
It takes extreme heat, and several hours of
exposure at that, to cut even the smallest

00:05:38.439 --> 00:05:41.439
portion of metal from the main bulk of SCP-882.

00:05:41.439 --> 00:05:43.749
But where did it come from?

00:05:43.749 --> 00:05:49.399
The SCP Foundation first recovered SCP-882
near an island community on the north east

00:05:49.399 --> 00:05:54.340
coast of Banks Island, one of the larger islands
in the Canadian Arctic Archipelago.

00:05:54.340 --> 00:05:59.310
Strangely, not a single scrap of metal, not
even underground metallic ore was found within

00:05:59.310 --> 00:06:03.199
a one mile radius of where the machine was
discovered.

00:06:03.199 --> 00:06:08.350
Stranger still, the small town located nearby
seemed to be abandoned, with signs that it

00:06:08.350 --> 00:06:12.749
had been devoid of any human life for quite
a number of years.

00:06:12.749 --> 00:06:18.969
The collection of fused metal components,
later designated SCP-882, was found submerged

00:06:18.969 --> 00:06:20.189
in sea water.

00:06:20.189 --> 00:06:24.879
The machine was coated in rust, and the Foundation
has chosen to keep it in in this same rusty

00:06:24.879 --> 00:06:28.389
state the whole time it has been kept in since
its containment.

00:06:28.389 --> 00:06:29.389
Why?

00:06:29.389 --> 00:06:34.759
Because when Foundation personnel first attempted
to remove SCP-882 from the water, and the

00:06:34.759 --> 00:06:40.809
rust began to flake away from SCP-882’s
metal surface, its gears and cogs started

00:06:40.809 --> 00:06:42.089
to turn.

00:06:42.089 --> 00:06:46.439
Foundation personnel on site were unsure of
what the machine’s purpose was, but wanted

00:06:46.439 --> 00:06:48.729
to halt it in case it proved deadly.

00:06:48.729 --> 00:06:53.249
A number of ill-fated attempts at containment
occurred soon after, with any person getting

00:06:53.249 --> 00:06:58.869
too close to SCP-882 finding themselves pulled
into its mass and crushed to death between

00:06:58.869 --> 00:07:00.649
turning cogs.

00:07:00.649 --> 00:07:05.169
After multiple accidents that resulted in
the demise of Foundation personnel, Doctor

00:07:05.169 --> 00:07:14.219
Charles Gears, authorized the use of SCP-2519
to help stop the movement of SCP-882’s gears.

00:07:14.219 --> 00:07:20.699
SCP-2519 is an audio file titled ‘Babylon.mp3’,
which features the song ‘By the waters of

00:07:20.699 --> 00:07:25.619
Babylon’ by Philip Hayes and text from the
biblical Psalm 137.

00:07:25.619 --> 00:07:30.090
Playing this file can cause malfunctions to
occur in various electronic and mechanical

00:07:30.090 --> 00:07:35.580
devices, normally reducing the speed at which
they can operate, or causing a complete cessation

00:07:35.580 --> 00:07:37.229
of a machine’s function.

00:07:37.229 --> 00:07:43.229
In SCP-882’s case, the sound of Babylon.mp3
successfully slowed the machine’s moving

00:07:43.229 --> 00:07:47.849
parts, allowing Foundation personnel to safely
get closer to it.

00:07:47.849 --> 00:07:53.149
Teams then cut the mass of metal down to a
more manageable size with extreme heat, and

00:07:53.149 --> 00:07:55.020
it was finally contained.

00:07:55.020 --> 00:07:57.449
However, another question arises.

00:07:57.449 --> 00:08:02.520
Surely, if SCP-882 is a machine, then it must
have a purpose, right?

00:08:02.520 --> 00:08:07.319
And, perhaps more importantly, what is its
connection to the infamous machine loving

00:08:07.319 --> 00:08:11.159
group of interest, The Church of the Broken
God?

00:08:11.159 --> 00:08:14.800
Both of these questions might have have one
easy answer.

00:08:14.800 --> 00:08:21.479
To put it plain and simple: SCP 882 may just
be the heart of The Broken God.

00:08:21.479 --> 00:08:25.860
The Church of The Broken God is a religious
organization that the SCP Foundation has had

00:08:25.860 --> 00:08:28.749
a number of encounters with over the years.

00:08:28.749 --> 00:08:33.210
Members of the Church share in the belief
that life, specifically biological flesh based

00:08:33.210 --> 00:08:36.839
life, is inherently wrong, even evil.

00:08:36.839 --> 00:08:42.409
This group worships mechanization, the process
of making something, or someone, more mechanical

00:08:42.409 --> 00:08:43.729
in nature.

00:08:43.729 --> 00:08:48.779
According to the beliefs of the Church, there
were two gods: Yaldabaoth and Mekhane, who

00:08:48.779 --> 00:08:50.320
created humanity together.

00:08:50.320 --> 00:08:55.500
Yaldabaoth was the god of flesh and animal
instinct, granting humans their bodies, while

00:08:55.500 --> 00:09:00.819
Mekhane, the god of machine and intellect,
blessed man with the power of free thought.

00:09:00.819 --> 00:09:05.770
As humankind developed and its civilizations
began building machines, Yaldabaoth became

00:09:05.770 --> 00:09:09.730
enraged that they were ignoring the instincts
she had bestowed upon them.

00:09:09.730 --> 00:09:14.350
She endeavored to destroy the creations of
man, in an attempt to revert them to the animals

00:09:14.350 --> 00:09:16.380
she had intended them to be.

00:09:16.380 --> 00:09:22.110
As the legend goes, Mekhane acted as humanity’s
savior, and intervened to stop Yaldabaoth.

00:09:22.110 --> 00:09:26.790
The god of machines shattered himself, transforming
his body into a number of pieces to form a

00:09:26.790 --> 00:09:28.870
cage for his fellow god.

00:09:28.870 --> 00:09:31.870
Fragments of Mekhane rained down on planet
Earth.

00:09:31.870 --> 00:09:36.130
Fragments that the Church of the Broken God
believe it is their duty to recover.

00:09:36.130 --> 00:09:37.130
There could potentially be hundreds of pieces
needed to rebuild Mekhane so he can lead the

00:09:37.130 --> 00:09:38.130
Church to glory and defeat Yaldabaoth once
and for all.

00:09:38.130 --> 00:09:41.550
However, a number of these pieces are catalogued
SCPs that the Foundation is either aware of,

00:09:41.550 --> 00:09:43.400
or has in containment.

00:09:43.400 --> 00:09:50.430
They are SCP-882, or ‘His Broken Heart’
to the Church, SCP-271, “His Broken Gift”,

00:09:50.430 --> 00:09:58.149
SCP-813, “His Broken Eyes”, SCP-1139,
“His Broken Tongue”, SCP-635, “His Broken

00:09:58.149 --> 00:10:04.279
Mind”, and finally His Broken Blood, which
refers to SCP-217.

00:10:04.279 --> 00:10:08.920
Often using anomalous technology, members
of the Church of The Broken God intend to

00:10:08.920 --> 00:10:12.160
uncover or steal these various components.

00:10:12.160 --> 00:10:16.610
The Church’s ultimate goal is to bring the
correct pieces together and completely restore

00:10:16.610 --> 00:10:17.610
Mekhane’s form.

00:10:17.610 --> 00:10:22.430
It is their hope that he will guide them to
intellectual enlightenment, and bless them

00:10:22.430 --> 00:10:27.829
with new, mechanical forms so that they can
discard their current, flesh and blood bodies.

00:10:27.829 --> 00:10:32.730
However, the Foundation and the Church are
certainly not the only groups to have a fascination

00:10:32.730 --> 00:10:35.139
with SCP-882.

00:10:35.139 --> 00:10:39.540
Near the Banks Island site where the machine
was first discovered, Foundation personnel

00:10:39.540 --> 00:10:43.990
encountered a man, the sole survivor of the
nearby town.

00:10:43.990 --> 00:10:48.389
This individual, by the name of Richard Wright,
was apprehended, and brought in for questioning

00:10:48.389 --> 00:10:50.190
with Doctor Gears.

00:10:50.190 --> 00:10:54.279
During their interview, Richard revealed a
number of details about the townsfolk who

00:10:54.279 --> 00:10:59.990
had first uncovered SCP-882, and what ultimately
became of them.

00:10:59.990 --> 00:11:05.510
According to his account, the community formed
a cult around SCP-882 after a man named Allen

00:11:05.510 --> 00:11:06.510
found it.

00:11:06.510 --> 00:11:11.019
The machine’s parts had begun to turn and
move, but with no clear indication as to what

00:11:11.019 --> 00:11:12.310
was powering it.

00:11:12.310 --> 00:11:18.009
Soon, a local priest, Father Pat, also took
an interest in SCP-882.

00:11:18.009 --> 00:11:22.069
Both he and Allen seemed to share a belief
that the machine had been built by God for

00:11:22.069 --> 00:11:26.620
a higher purpose, and encouraged residents
of the nearby town to come and offer metal

00:11:26.620 --> 00:11:27.620
to it.

00:11:27.620 --> 00:11:31.480
Richard explained that the locals were plagued
by the auditory hallucinations typical of

00:11:31.480 --> 00:11:38.050
long term exposure to SCP-882, kept awake
at all hours of the night by clanking, grinding,

00:11:38.050 --> 00:11:39.470
and the screaming of metal.

00:11:39.470 --> 00:11:44.551
Before long, Richard noticed more and more
metal items being fed to the machine, with

00:11:44.551 --> 00:11:48.639
many local residents content to just sit and
stare at the mass.

00:11:48.639 --> 00:11:54.100
He also noted that Father Pat and Allen both
seemed to be acting strangely around the machine,

00:11:54.100 --> 00:11:58.259
insisting that all the metal that had been
added to it still wasn’t enough.

00:11:58.259 --> 00:12:04.660
Then one night, during a communion before
SCP-882, Father Pat took a pair of pliers

00:12:04.660 --> 00:12:08.199
and began tearing out townspeople’s metal
fillings.

00:12:08.199 --> 00:12:13.250
Richard watched in horror as the priest wrenched
teeth from the mouths of ordinary people and

00:12:13.250 --> 00:12:18.040
threw them into SCP-882, but still claiming
it wasn’t enough.

00:12:18.040 --> 00:12:23.129
Then, he turned on Allen, accusing him of
hiding metal from the great machine inside

00:12:23.129 --> 00:12:24.129
his body.

00:12:24.129 --> 00:12:30.079
The townsfolk turned on Allen, the first one
to find SCP-882, and threw him and his metal

00:12:30.079 --> 00:12:35.129
hip into the machine, his body breaking under
its moving parts.

00:12:35.129 --> 00:12:41.190
Luckily, SCP-882 remains contained, at least
for now until the members of the Church of

00:12:41.190 --> 00:12:45.749
the Broken God find a way to reunite the heart
of their god with the other pieces of its

00:12:45.749 --> 00:12:51.120
scattered body and Mekhane can rise again
- an outcome that his worshippers are eager

00:12:51.120 --> 00:12:54.769
to bring to fruition sooner rather than later...

00:12:54.769 --> 00:13:01.680
Now check out “SCP-055 - Anti Meme / Unknown”
and “SCP-1981 - Ronald Reagan Cut Up While

00:13:01.680 --> 00:13:08.189
Talking &amp; SCP-095” for more SCP Foundation
rabbit holes from SCP Explained!

